caption: $:/tags/hypergsd/Review/*
title: Review blocks

! Summary
Add an entry to the Review sidebar — a link, a component, or any block-level content — placed in one of the numbered blocks.

! Detail
Tag a tiddler with `$:/tags/hypergsd/Review/<n>`:

```
title: $:/plugins/your-plugin/ui/sidebar/review/notes
tags: Documentation [[HyperGSD API]]

\whitespace trim
\procedure lingo-base() $:/language/hypergsd/Sidebar/

<$link to="GSD/Notes"><<lingo Review/Notes>></$link><br/>
```

* The number picks the block. Shipped blocks: ''1'' realm selection, ''2'' project links, ''3'' action links, ''4'' contexts and ticklers, ''5'' references, contacts and cleanup.
* Within-block order comes from the block tag tiddler's `list` field (the core convention) — listed entries render first in `list` order, unlisted ones append alphabetically.
* The entry's body is the content, rendered block-mode inside the block's `div`. Define your own `\procedure lingo-base()` if you use `<<lingo>>`.
* The blocks themselves are discovered from the tag tiddlers' titles, sorted numerically — ship a `$:/tags/hypergsd/Review/6` tiddler to open a sixth block.
* An absent sub-plugin is simply a missing entry; nothing gates on plugin existence.
* The gap between blocks is one stylesheet rule (`.hgsd-review-block + .hgsd-review-block`); blocks carry no other styling, so your entry inherits the sidebar's.

! Best Practice
Keep entries to one line of content plus a trailing `<br/>` to match the shipped rhythm; anything taller belongs on the page it links to.